Frozen prototype text
=====================

The parity checks compare what Kira ships against the research prototype that produced
the published measurements. That prototype is a private tree: it is not published, and
it will not sit beside a clone of this repository. Frozen here are exactly the files
those checks open, byte for byte, in the layout they have there — so the comparison
runs from this artifact alone rather than skipping on every machine but the author's.

Frozen from
-----------

source: k8s-agentic-operator (private)
commit: 30070ee38b5d87327b70280520d219a887f8ff1a
date: 2026-09-07

Three files were taken from that checkout's working tree rather than from the commit,
and a refreeze from a clean clone of 30070ee will not reproduce them:

  agent/prompts/verify.txt                                 uncommitted, +2 lines
  agent/tools/registry.py                                  uncommitted, +59/-3 lines
  agent/prompts/runtime/roles/verify/submit_without_entry_point.txt   untracked

They are frozen as they were because that working tree is what the shipped assets were
migrated from and what the checks were passing against. Recording it here is the point:
the alternative is a copy that says "commit 30070ee" and silently is not.

What is here
------------

The 75 prompt assets test_prompt_assets.py maps a shipped asset back to, the tool
registry test_toolsets.py parses AGENT_TOOLSETS out of, and the projection renderer
test_projections.py re-derives its golden file by running. Nothing else of the
prototype: tests/unit/test_frozen_prototype.py fails on a file the checks read that is
missing here, and on a file here that no check reads.

Three of those assets are the AIOpsLab adapter's, which ships its prompts inside its own
package rather than under src/kira/prompts. They are frozen at the layout they have in
the prototype, agent/prompts/runtime/aiopslab/, like every other file here.

The prototype sources of the assets in test_prompt_assets.DELIBERATELY_DIVERGED are
absent on purpose. That check skips before reading them, so freezing them would vendor
text nothing compares — the divergence itself is documented at each entry.

Refreezing
----------

Point KIRA_PROTOTYPE_ROOT at a prototype checkout and confirm the checks still pass
against it, which is what says the frozen copy and its source have not drifted apart:

    KIRA_PROTOTYPE_ROOT=<checkout> uv run pytest tests/unit/test_prompt_assets.py \
        tests/unit/test_projections.py tests/unit/test_toolsets.py

Then copy the same set forward and update commit, date and the exceptions above:

    uv run python - <<'PY'
    import shutil, sys
    from pathlib import Path
    sys.path.insert(0, "tests/unit")
    from prototype_tree import FROZEN
    from test_frozen_prototype import COMPARED
    live = Path("<checkout>")
    for relative in COMPARED:
        (FROZEN / relative).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        shutil.copyfile(live / relative, FROZEN / relative)
    PY

A refreeze that copies part of the set fails test_frozen_prototype rather than passing
quietly with the checks reading two prototype revisions at once.
